1
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,460
How can you sleep on a bamboo mat
in silk clothes?

2
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,040
Take it off.

3
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:55,600
What for?

4
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,780
Cotton should be fine to sleep in.

5
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:04,440
This is Shen Feng,
the head chef of Yunbianshang.

6
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,720
He specially prepared

7
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,850
some local specialties for everyone.

8
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,479
This is fermented amaranth stems.

9
00:02:10,479 --> 00:02:12,360
It's made by cutting amaranth stems
into sections, soaking them,

10
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,880
and letting them ferment naturally.

11
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,740
It tastes sour and tender,
with a unique fragrance.

12
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,160
This is

13
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,520
stinky tofu soaked in amaranth juice.

14
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,640
Compared to other places,

15
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,100
it has a different flavor.

16
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,079
That one is Daodu vegetable.

17
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:27,079
It's made from nine-headed mustard,

18
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:29,360
pressed upside down into a clay jar,
and sealed for half a year.

19
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:31,620
It's sour, refreshing, and appetizing.

20
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,120
Sounds very novel.

21
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,240
Then give it a try.

22
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,220
Try it quickly.

23
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,640
How is it?

24
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,520
It's so delicious!

25
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,720
This taste is quite unique.

26
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,650
It definitely goes well with rice.

27
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,600
What on earth is this?

28
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:52,200
It's not only salty but also stinky.

29
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,240
Our Chef Shen's culinary skills

30
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,700
are universally praised.

31
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,040
Mr. Hu,

32
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,000
different regions

33
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,360
have different survival genes.

34
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,200
Some are good at
domesticating wild beasts,

35
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,060
some excel at cultivating crops,

36
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,840
and the wisdom of our nation

37
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,600
lies in taming and cultivating

38
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,570
these invisible microorganisms.

39
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:14,080
They are actually not just food,

40
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,160
but a kind of history and heritage.

41
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,520
What we eat

42
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,400
is not just a flavor,

43
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,680
but a culture.

44
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,400
Tasting it like this,

45
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,040
it's indeed extraordinary.

46
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:32,800
You see,

47
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,160
what we are tasting is not just flavor,

48
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,600
but

49
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,640
a cultural

50
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,680
resonance.

51
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:46,120
We are not eating simple food,

52
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:51,000
but the crystallization of the wisdom
of working people over thousands of years,

53
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:54,280
a historical relic

54
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:56,960
flowing on the tip of the tongue.

55
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,480
Exactly. Brilliant insight, Mr. Hu.

56
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,760
You two,

57
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,020
please have a seat.

58
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,130
We can't have you standing
and serving us the whole time.

59
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,960
For some, it's not about the taste,
but the story.

60
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,240
So pretentious.

61
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,580
Since everyone's here today,

62
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,960
let's stick to the old rules

63
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,880
and play an icebreaker

64
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,160
to liven things up.

65
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:21,120
It'll also help Hu

66
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,920
fit into our team faster.

67
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,800
She just got here
and hasn't played this before.

68
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,360
Yun,

69
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,200
you're a veteran here.

70
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,500
You know this best.

71
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,960
Let's start with Truth, alright?

72
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:33,960
Zhang Jian,

73
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,200
you kick it off.

74
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,200
So the first question is,

75
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:42,880
when were everyone's 'three firsts'?

76
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:47,200
Are the 'three firsts'...

77
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:51,520
First love, first kiss,
and first time, right?

78
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,760
Exactly.

79
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,740
I know Qingqing's.

80
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,600
She mentioned her first love

81
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,840
when she just joined.

82
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,080
I made that up.

83
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,820
You actually believed it?

84
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,720
You lied during Truth or Dare?

85
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,730
Since you made it up before,

86
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,280
just gather your courage
and tell us today.

87
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:13,080
Perfect timing to set an example for Hu.

88
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,440
You're so eager.

89
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,100
Why don't you set the example?

90
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,520
Have you bought a house?

91
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,080
Bought a car?

92
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,770
What's your salary?

93
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,760
Paid off your online loans yet?

94
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,720
That bracelet looks pretty real.

95
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,650
Where did you get the knockoff?

96
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,240
You look pale,

97
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:34,440
and your vibe is just so-so.

98
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,320
You must be pretty weak.

99
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,720
W-W-Why bring all this up?

100
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:40,940
Next question.

101
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,120
Next game.

102
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,159
Let's play

103
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,920
the chest-bumping balloon game.

104
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,640
Two people per team.

105
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,840
Let's see which team is the fastest
and pops the most.

106
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:52,400
Alright.

107
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:54,000
Come on, Qing, let's team up.

108
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,960
This game is best played
with a guy and a girl.

109
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:57,680
Mr. Hu,

110
00:05:58,159 --> 00:06:00,080
this game is fun. Let's go first.

111
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:03,840
One more.

112
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:04,600
Again?

113
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:08,000
Let's do it.

114
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:08,720
Again?

115
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,520
One more.

116
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,560
Come on, Mr. Hu.

117
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,880
Come on, Mr. Hu.

118
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,320
Mr. Hu,

119
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,280
What's wrong, Mr. Hu?

120
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:23,760
Are you okay?

121
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,820
What are you doing?

122
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:26,840
You're not mad, are you, Mr. Hu?

123
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,280
I'm not mad.

124
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,880
What a huge mountain.

125
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:30,960
That really hurt.

126
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,320
How can I eat? The food is getting cold.

127
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,320
Let's eat.

128
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,920
Okay, okay.

129
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:37,560
Eat up. It's getting cold.

130
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,480
Today was so satisfying.

131
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,400
Yeah.

132
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,480
It's my first time seeing

133
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,600
Hu Zhang fall so hard on his butt.

134
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:57,960
You've got some nice pecs. Pretty firm.

135
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,159
You're not bad yourself.

136
00:06:59,159 --> 00:07:01,800
When I first saw you acting
so submissive to Hu Zhang,

137
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,680
I thought you were quite a pushover.

138
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,640
I didn't expect you
to finally muster the courage

139
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,570
to fight back for that little girl.

140
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,640
Actually, I've played that game before.

141
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,400
When I first joined the company,

142
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,680
I had to bite the bullet just to fit in.

143
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:17,000
Seeing Xiao Hu like that just now,

144
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,200
I felt like I was looking at my past self.

145
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,440
Trembling with fear,

146
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,770
yet not daring to say no.

147
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,380
Let me tell you,

148
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,040
if someone had stood up

149
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,560
to help me back then,

150
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,280
I would have been so grateful to them.

151
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,320
So today,

152
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,960
I wanted to be the person
I once hoped for.

153
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,760
Besides, I've already quit.

154
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,180
I'm not afraid of them.

155
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,880
If your former company was so awful,

156
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,480
why didn't you quit sooner?

157
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,720
Actually, many companies are the same.

158
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,320
It's like a huge,

159
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,120
disgusting obedience test.

160
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,040
Either you join them in their dirty deeds,

161
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,920
or you pack up and leave.

162
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:56,080
Then it's actually a good thing
you left the company.

163
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:56,940
Think about it.

164
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,440
Your values were fundamentally at odds

165
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,840
with your former bosses.

166
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,560
And you couldn't comfortably

167
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,000
go along with them like Zhang Jian did.

168
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,240
Staying there would only

169
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,500
make you more and more miserable, right?

170
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:13,600
Actually, when I first quit,

171
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,920
I was quite sad.

172
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,720
I felt like a total failure.

173
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,280
But now I understand.

174
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,960
I was just in a dump.

175
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,520
No matter how hard I tried,

176
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,880
those pieces of trash
would never understand,

177
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,760
recognize, or validate me.

178
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,960
It's not that I wasn't good enough,

179
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,560
it's because they are trash.

180
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,000
And I used to think

181
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,480
everything had to have a meaning,

182
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,159
a purpose, a result.

183
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:36,880
Not only did work need KPIs,

184
00:08:36,919 --> 00:08:38,520
but life needed KPIs too.

185
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,720
But what exactly is success

186
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,400
for ordinary people like us?

187
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,559
A good job,

188
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:44,720
a good marriage,

189
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,720
and having a good child.

190
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,050
Is that what success is?

191
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:51,960
These things are like invisible whips,

192
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,810
constantly lashing our backs,

193
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,380
making us go faster

194
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,760
and faster.

195
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,200
Living this aimless life now

196
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,320
is so relaxing.

197
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,920
I can waste time without any burden,

198
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,880
and I can do

199
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,520
meaningless things to my heart's content.

200
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,280
I can be a mindless

201
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,840
but happy loser.

202
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,120
Exactly.

203
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,160
We are here to experience this world.

204
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,960
Don't wrong yourself

205
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:18,360
for the sake of success in others' eyes.

206
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:20,560
By the way,

207
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,920
you lost our bet.

208
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:23,800
Now, not only has Ms. Shu

209
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,560
moved into Yue Shanchuan's house,

210
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:26,800
she's also sleeping in the master bedroom.

211
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,530
How about that? Do you concede?

212
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,840
Looks like Shanchuan
really messed up this time.

213
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,040
I think so too.

214
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,600
Why the sudden lightning?

215
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,840
Is it going to rain?

216
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:41,840
Good thing I brought an umbrella.

217
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,970
Wait for me a second.

218
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,560
Ten fragments. A bet is a bet.

219
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,730
Isn't this trick a bit old-fashioned?

220
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,560
It doesn't matter

221
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:31,680
as long as it works.

222
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,720
Fine.

223
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,400
It's so late. Why aren't you asleep?

224
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,220
I haven't finished my work for today.

225
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,760
Spreadsheets again.

226
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:12,600
If there's anything you don't understand,
just ask me.

227
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,120
I'm familiar with this.

228
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,000
Staring at the screen this late

229
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,240
must be hard on your eyes.

230
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,000
A little.

231
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,420
Eat this. It's good for your eyes.

232
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:23,600
Thanks.

233
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:27,280
But these are just boring,
repetitive tasks.

234
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,520
Not difficult,

235
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:29,940
just time-consuming.

236
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,440
When I first graduated,

237
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,640
I always thought
company meetings were like

238
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,520
a clash of ideas

239
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:39,240
and brainstorming among elites.

240
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,920
But after I started working,

241
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:44,490
I realized it's just a huge
blame-shifting conference,

242
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:47,320
distributing the amount of blame
everyone has to take.

243
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,120
Studying hard for over a decade,

244
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:49,960
only to end up

245
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,920
doing boring and meaningless work

246
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:53,280
day after day.

247
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,540
If I had known this,

248
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:57,500
I might as well have frozen to death
while studying.

249
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:04,680
This time last year,
I was still in France,

250
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:07,320
copying art murals in Commercy.

251
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:09,920
You studied art?

252
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,160
I've been studying oil painting
since I was a kid.

253
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:13,720
When I was little,

254
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,920
I always dreamed of becoming a painter.

255
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:19,640
Painting has always been my dream.

256
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,520
But to my parents,

257
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,600
it was just a bonus point

258
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:25,120
to get into a good college.

259
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,720
I don't really have much talent anyway.

260
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:30,480
I probably wouldn't make much money
or fame from painting.

261
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:33,560
I could only barely support myself.

262
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:35,280
So they thought

263
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,920
I definitely needed

264
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,840
a stable and decent job.

265
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,480
But this company

266
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:45,320
isn't exactly a top-tier firm.

267
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,560
Is it worth giving up your dream for?

268
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,840
So they arranged for me to come here

269
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,040
to gain some experience,

270
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:53,840
to make it easier
to go to a bigger company later.

271
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:57,480
I know they mean well,

272
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:00,720
but I know in my heart
this isn't what I want.

273
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,520
And I'm not happy at all.

274
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:06,720
Do you know

275
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,320
how many people would kill for

276
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,680
the things you don't want?

277
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,480
You could study art

278
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,560
and go abroad to paint for your dream.

279
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:14,720
For someone like me from a poor family,

280
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,600
I could only study desperately on my own.

281
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,160
After graduation, I had no resources
and no connections.

282
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,880
I had to find a job all by myself.

283
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,480
Even the company you look down on,

284
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,280
I had to fight tooth and nail

285
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,200
to get into.

286
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,000
I don't even know

287
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,040
what you're being so sentimental about.

288
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,120
Even a nobody like me hasn't cried.

289
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,000
I work cautiously every day,

290
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,480
watching your uncle's mood.

291
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,240
I'm terrified that one day

292
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,480
I'll make a mistake and get laid off.

293
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:37,400
If I could stay in the company
for the rest of my life,

294
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:39,280
that would be a good ending.

295
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:43,520
Fang Yuan, I can understand how you feel.

296
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:46,000
But everyone's pain is different.

297
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,800
Yes, you're in pain.

298
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,330
But to me, you're just being dramatic.

299
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,080
Everyone is born different

300
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,570
and has different things to overcome.

301
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:11,080
She's just too repressed and miserable.

302
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,300
Don't take it to heart.

303
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,520
It's late. Get some rest.

304
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,530
I'm going to bed.

305
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,320
Good night.
